Z||000000||ezsurf||07-29-99||08:30 PM||||<br>When is the radiator fan supposed to come on?  Mine comes on as soon as I turn the ignition key to on (before the engine is started).  I believe it has been rewired.  There are three wires wrapped with duct tape.  
Z||000001||JetroGT||07-29-99||09:23 PM||||That fan is only supposed to come on when you turn on your air, or if the coolent temp becomes too hot.
Z||000002||ChadMan||07-30-99||07:04 AM||||In my V6 car, the fan doesn't come on until the "overheat" light is already flickering.  I can also turn it on by turning on my (nonfunctional) A/C.<p>I remember Paul saying in another thread that he wired his own switch to turn on the fan.  I have to track down some other electrical bugs this weekend and might try that myself.
Z||000003||ChadMan||07-30-99||07:05 AM||||Sorry, I was just rambling.  Yeah, ez, sounds like somebody has rewired your fan so it would come on whenever the ignition's on.  Probably because the damn thing wouldn't come on until the car's about to overheat!
Z||000004||ezsurf||07-30-99||07:23 AM||||I guess I'll just leave it that way , unless someone knows of some reason that it's a bad idea.  The only thing I can think of is that the fan will wear out quicker.
Z||000005||Nick||07-30-99||11:44 AM||||I seem to remember somebody saying that having the fan run all the time was bad.  I can't recall the exact reasons why, but it had something to do with the ECM making the car run in warm-up mode all the time.  I am not sure if this is right.  <p>What I want to know is if there is another way to get the fan to kick on earlier, WITHOUT wiring a switch, or wiring it to run all the time.  I have emailed Hypertech about their low temp. fan switch, but haven't gotten any responses yet.  
